  "title": "BNCI 2014-002 Motor Imagery dataset",
  "description": "EEG recordings from 14 healthy participants performing a two-class motor imagery task (right hand versus feet) using a cue-guided Graz-BCI paradigm with continuous visual bar-graph feedback. Data were acquired from 15 EEG channels at 512 Hz over 8 runs, totalling 160 trials per subject in a single session. The dataset supports benchmarking of sensorimotor rhythm BCI classifiers such as random forests and shrinkage LDA.",
  "methods_description": "EEG was recorded with g.USBamp amplifiers and active Ag/AgCl electrodes (g.LADYbird caps) in a Laplacian montage, referenced to the left mastoid and grounded at the right mastoid, using BCI2000. Data were sampled at 512 Hz and online filtered with 8th-order Butterworth band-pass filters. Each session consisted of 8 runs with 160 trials (80 right hand, 80 feet) and 5 s motor imagery periods with continuous feedback.",
